<problem>
<!-- <title>Solution to linear discrete dynamical system, fraction rate of change</title> -->

<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="a" from="2" to=" 10" />
<selectFromSequence name="b" from="10" to=" 100" step=" 10" />
<select name="x">x y z s u v w </select>
<select name="n">n t </select>
<math name="answer" simplify="full">(1/$a )**$n *$b </math>

</setup>

<p>Compute the solution to the discrete dynamical system</p>

<md>
<mrow> $(x)_{ $n + 1 }\amp = \frac{1}{$a} $(x)_$n</mrow>
<mrow> $(x)_0\amp = $b </mrow>
</md>

<p><m>$x _$n  =</m> 
<answer>
<award>$answer </award>
</answer>
</p>


<solution>
In each time step <m>$x </m> is multiplied by <m>\frac{1}{ $a  }</m>.  To go from the initial condition <m>$x _0 = $b </m> to <m>$x _$n </m>, we must multiply by <m>\frac{1}{ $a  }</m> a total of <m>$n </m> times, or multiply by <m>\left(\frac{1}{ $a  }\right)^$n </m>.  The solution is <m>$x _$n =$answer </m>.


</solution>


</problem>